  "scope": "Actual source gate acceptance derives local hereditary plain annotations and empty physical own fields from initial coherence and availability. Initial endpoint descendant exclusion derives a finite selected-value Cap at its payload mass; the actual primary endpoint trace supplies this exclusion. No whole-input Cap or whole-forest closure premise is added. Ordinary Required returns retain original row guards, symbols, and arities. Actual plain unfolding, Head, and Required retain zero-own-field annotations at the same returned heaps. These read-preservation results do not construct general outer completion. A source-built primary-admitted parent run raises edge height2 to3 and returns a child of height3 equal to the initial parent node. The same fixture completes a literal outer call and retains an exact ready B cell. It demonstrates copying and finite memo reuse, not divergence or a Haskell defect. General nonempty live walks, rows, ordinary nodes, causal returned-child progress, owner busy exclusion, repeated-pass convergence, current Haskell adapters, lazy forcing and publication, concrete memo events, host capacity, and complete public correspondence remain open. The whole-library goal remains active."
